; arm64_boot_smoke.simi — M4b + M5.2 contention probe (plan doc §6 M4 /
; §10.187, §6 M5.2 / §10.196): the program embedded into
; kernel/kernel_arm64.c's boot-time smoke test. Originally the M4b
; trivial 42-return mirror of rv64_boot_smoke.simi; the M5.2
; contention probe (Phase 9n-style, §10.196) makes it a LONG-RUNNING
; loop so a tick can fire INSIDE each EL0 excursion's window — the
; kernel's own logs prove the pended tick is taken exactly once on the
; svc-return to EL1 (unbroken [TICK N] stream, zero lost ticks, zero
; missed re-arms). The loop count (1e8) is chosen so the window
; comfortably exceeds the 100 ms tick period across realistic TCG
; speeds: the emitted A64 loop body is ~10 instructions per SIMI
; iteration (the block-head frame reload), so 1e8 iterations is ~1e9
; A64 instructions — measured ~0.5 s per EL0 window on the dev host
; (a ~5x margin vs the 100 ms period; the total boot is ~3 s, far
; under the CI 60 s timeout even at 5x slower TCG). The margin is the
; whole point: if an EL0 window ever dropped BELOW the period, a
; level-sensitive tick would deassert before being taken and the gate
; would lose it (the exact failure this probe exists to prove absent).
; The result is still 42, so the M4b/M5.1 gates (four entries, one
; translation, all 42) are unchanged. The execution benches
; (bench-exec & friends) SKIP this fixture: it is kernel-embedded, not
; a parity-corpus fixture, and a 500x bench-exec run of the loop would
; take ~an hour (see §10.196). The size gate passes --max-steps to
; raise the verifier's 10M step budget for this one row.
; Expected result: 42
.entry main
main:
    ENTER #4
    LOADI r0, #0, i32        ; counter
    LOADI r1, #100000000, i32 ; limit — the loop window (see above)
    LOADI r2, #1, i32        ; step
loop:
    ADD r0, r0, r2, i32
    CMP r3, r0, r1, i32, LT
    BC r3, loop
    LOADI r0, #42, i32
    RET
